Package: cloud-apt-hello
Version: 0.2.0-1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: cloud-apt example <noreply@example.com>
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6
Description: cloud-apt namespaced hello example
 A minimal C program packaged as a .deb to demonstrate the
 cloud-apt repository workflow. The package is intentionally
 named 'cloud-apt-hello' (not 'hello') to avoid conflicting
 with the official Debian 'hello' package in main (which
 prints 'Hello, world!' and is used for dpkg/apt smoke tests).
 .
 Installs /opt/cloud-apt-hello-0.2.0/bin/cloud-apt-hello and
 exposes it via /usr/local/bin/cloud-apt-hello. Supports
 --version, --repo, and --help flags for verifying which
 version is installed and which repository it came from.
